## What companies expect today

For **software engineering roles**:

* Programming language proficiency (Python, Java, C++, C#, etc.)
* Data Structures & Algorithms
* Problem-solving
* Object-Oriented Programming
* SQL (many roles)
* System Design (mid/senior levels)

For **AI/GenAI roles**, companies may additionally assess:

* Python
* Machine Learning basics
* LLM APIs
* RAG
* Vector Databases
* AI Agents
* Prompt Engineering
* MCP and tool calling
* Model evaluation and debugging



So, while programming has been part of technical interviews since the **1970s–1980s**, the **modern online coding assessment** 
format used by companies like TCS and Microsoft became widespread during the **late 2000s and 2010s**.





